## Why This Implementation Matters

- Smooth animation: render updates with [requestAnimationFrame](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Window/requestAnimationFrame)
- Stays attached during fast movement with [setPointerCapture](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/setPointerCapture)
- Keeps working even while scrolling thanks to the [scroll](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document/scroll_event) event handler
- Simple cleanup by listening for [lostpointercapture](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/lostpointercapture_event) and calling [releasePointerCapture](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/releasePointerCapture)

Because I apply `touch-action: none` for touch devices, make sure you copy the CSS from the [CodePen demo](https://codepen.io/nishinoshake/pen/jEWVJqG) when you reuse this.

CodePen Embed - Smooth Draggable Element with Scroll Support

```
<div class="stage">
  <div class="draggable"></div>
</div>
```

```
body {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
}

.stage {
  width: 100vw;
  height: 100vh;
  padding-right: 200vw;
  padding-bottom: 200vh;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  box-sizing: content-box;
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #f0f9ff 0%, #e0f2fe 50%, #bae6fd 100%);
  box-shadow: inset 0 15px 40px rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.2);
}

.draggable {
  position: relative;
  width: 72px;
  aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
  touch-action: none;
  cursor: grab;
  transition: transform 120ms ease-out;
}

.draggable:before {
  content: "";
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  border-radius: 16px;
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #5e6cf3 0%, #c0c6ff 100%);
  box-shadow: 0 15px 35px rgba(65, 79, 195, 0.35);
  transition: box-shadow 200ms ease-out, transform 200ms ease-out;
}

/* Expand the interactive area for easier grabbing */
.draggable:after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  display: block;
  transform: scale(1.2);
}

.draggable.is-dragging {
  cursor: grabbing;
  will-change: transform;
}

.draggable.is-dragging:before {
  box-shadow: 0 20px 45px rgba(47, 63, 182, 0.45);
  transform: scale(0.9);
}

/* On iOS, transitions during drag feel a bit weird and uncomfortable. */
@supports (-webkit-touch-callout: none) {
  .draggable {
    transition: 0s;
  }
}
